{"id": "sdqa0102", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3375832760, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "55d54790f4984a1399d890ed29cf337bf030dd977d2cbf354d2e7727784c1c44", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "What was the world champion rugby team in 2018?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0102.wav", "input_sha256": "ee6796e32537a56701a1b1b094c68c81828f311dce4e35aefd1f0b548ba3e924", "input_samples": 111514, "input_s": 6.97, "n_real_chunks": 7, "score": 0.8274, "act": 0.9999, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "There was no Rugby World Cup champion in 2018 for the main 15-a-side men’s Rugby World Cup—the tournaments were in 2015 and 2019. , 2015 Rugby World Cup champion: New Zealand , 2019 Rugby World Cup champion: South Africa If you mean the 2018 Rugby World Cup Sevens, the champions were New Zealand in both the men’s and women’s tournaments.", "expert_answer": "There was **no Rugby World Cup champion in 2018** for the main 15-a-side men’s Rugby World Cup—the tournaments were in **2015** and **2019**.\n\n- **2015 Rugby World Cup champion:** **New Zealand**\n- **2019 Rugby World Cup champion:** **South Africa**\n\nIf you mean the **2018 Rugby World Cup Sevens**, the champions were **New Zealand** in both the men’s and women’s tournaments.", "transcript": "What was the world champion rugby team in 2018?\n", "asr_s": 0.7, "expert_s": 4.03, "expert_input_samples": 111514, "expert_input_s": 6.97, "expert_input_sha256": "ee6796e32537a56701a1b1b094c68c81828f311dce4e35aefd1f0b548ba3e924", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.097, "relay_synth_ms": 12444, "onset_chunk": 6, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/da